# politicas — environment variables (template)
#
# This file documents variable NAMES only. It contains NO secrets and NO real
# values. Copy to `.env.local` for local dev (git-ignored), and set the real
# values in the Vercel dashboard for Production and Preview environments
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables). See docs/deploy/vercel.md.
#
# Every var below is OPTIONAL: with none set, the app runs normally and Sentry
# is a completely silent no-op (no init, no network, no console noise).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry — error & performance monitoring (client + server)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN — the single gate for ALL Sentry activity.
#   Unset  → Sentry.init is never called anywhere (silent no-op).
#   Set    → client, server, and edge runtimes report to this DSN.
#   Public by design (embedded in the client bundle); not a secret.
#   Set the SAME value in Vercel Production and Preview.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV — environment tag attached to every Sentry event.
#   Suggested values, per Vercel environment:
#     Production → production
#     Preview    → preview
#     Local dev  → development
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry — build-time source-map upload (optional; CI / Vercel build only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed to un-minify stack traces in Sentry. If any are unset, the build
# skips source-map upload silently — it never fails the build. Do NOT commit a
# real SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN; set it only in Vercel (marked as a secret) and/or CI.

# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reviewer write path — /penize/kontrola human-verification console (Case ①)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gates the ONLY write path on the platform: confirming/rejecting a pending
# MP↔company tie. Single-operator console — one shared token, not per-user auth.
#   Unset REVIEWER_TOKEN → the write path is OFF; the console stays read-only
#   and states this honestly ("not-configured"), it never fails silently.
#   Set both → the console accepts decisions whose submitted token matches
#   REVIEWER_TOKEN exactly; REVIEWER_NAME is stamped as the reviewer on every
#   review_audit row and kg_edge.props update.
#   BOTH ARE REQUIRED TOGETHER (2026-08-04). With REVIEWER_TOKEN set but
#   REVIEWER_NAME unset the server REFUSES every decision ("misconfigured")
#   and the console says so before anything is written: decisions enter a
#   tamper-evident hash chain, and a chain that cannot say WHO decided is a
#   log, not an audit. It used to fall back to the literal name "reviewer".
# Server-only secrets — do NOT prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# REVIEWER_NAME=
# REVIEWER_TOKEN=
